# CODEOWNERS - require code-owner review on the authoritative corpus, its generated
# indexes, the builders, and CI. Enforced only when master branch protection has
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled.
# Last matching pattern wins. Owner is the GitHub user @nerdkim.
#
# This repository holds documents only: no application, no build output, no infra.
# So there is no /infra/ or /deploy/ entry here; every path below is corpus, or the
# tooling that guards it.

# CI (the docs workflow: conventions, corpus integrity, index drift) + this file
/.github/            @nerdkim

# The authoritative bilingual corpus. Korean is authoritative, English is an
# unofficial translation, and the two must change together.
/docs/               @nerdkim

# extended/manifest.json is a PUBLISHED CONTRACT read by nerdkim/security-criteria-web.
# A schema change here breaks that consumer, so it needs an owner review.
/extended/           @nerdkim

# The deterministic builders and the read-only integrity checker. CI regenerates with
# these and fails on any diff, so they define what "the indexes are correct" means.
/tools/              @nerdkim

# The playbook guard set (conventions checker, git hooks, hook installer)
/harness/            @nerdkim

# Source pin and the known-divergence register: records which official edition the
# corpus is based on, and which upstream legal changes are deliberately NOT reflected.
/UPDATES.md          @nerdkim
/UPDATES.ko.md       @nerdkim
